n of the Roland TR-808 drum machine and is closely associated with Hip Hop's formative years in the early to mid 1980s. It is not to be confused with electro house, which is commonly shortened to just \"electro\" in EDM circles. The electro style is defined by the 808 and 808 drum samples arranged in syncopated rhythm patterns often resembling the Funk breaks used in Hip Hop  beats with simple, funky basslines.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": 1329, "best_position": 89}, {"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": 1271, "best_position": 100}, {"artist": "2hollis", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Aphex Twin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Crystal Castles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Snow Strippers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electronic": {"genre": "electronic", "country_code": "ee", "country_name": "Estonia", "summary": "Electronic music refers to music that emphasizes the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic music technology as a central aspect of the sound of the music. Historically, electronic music was considered to be any music created with the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic processing, but in modern times, that distinction has been lost because almost all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 3069, "best_position": 55}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": 1454, "best_position": 69}, {"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": 1329, "best_position": 89}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": 1321, "best_position": 91}, {"artist":