, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": 3159, "best_position": 54}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 3069, "best_position": 55}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": 1564, "best_position": 58}, {"artist": "Mac Miller", "streams": 1538, "best_position": 61}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": 1454, "best_position": 69}, {"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": 1271, "best_position": 100}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bladee", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Eminem", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "metal": {"genre": "metal", "country_code": "ee", "country_name": "Estonia", "summary": "A metal is a material that exhibits a lustrous appearance when polished or fractured and conducts electricity and heat relatively efficiently. These properties are associated with the presence of electrons at the Fermi level. Metals are typically ductile, allowing them to be drawn into wires, and malleable, enabling them to be shaped by hammering or pressing.\n\nA metal may be a chemical element, such as iron, an alloy such as stainless steel, or a molecular compound such as polymeric sulfur nitride.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Bring Me the Horizon", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Limp Bizkit", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Metallica", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Nirvana", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Rammstein", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Red Hot Chili Peppers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Slipknot", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "System of a Down", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "new wave": {"genre": "new wave", "country_code": "ee", "country_name": "Estonia", "summary": "New wave is today a quite broad umbrella term describing popular music from around 1977 to 1986. But originally it was a slim sub genre of Western popular music that arose in the United Kingdom about 1977-78. It had close ties to punk rock and fairly strong influences of the musical style that had been invented and continuously developed throughout the 1970s: reggae.\n\nThe term new wave was first a kind of description of a more musical and lyric wise complex music than punk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "The Killers", "streams": 2003, "best_position": 29}, {"artist": "David Bowie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Depeche Mode", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Fontaines D.C.", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "MGMT", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Paramore", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Cure", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Strokes", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "nu metal": {"genre": "nu metal", "country_code": "ee", "country_name": "Estonia", "summary": "Nu metal is a subgenre of alternative metal that blends elements of heavy metal with influenc